andidate of the position is a cia agent  or something and this is the traditional  thing that that people say about this  regime that everybody is a member of the  sea that everything is a conspiracy and  i'm absolutely aware of the history you  know since walker invaded nicaragua in  the 19th century you want to talk about  invasions about u.s intervention nobody  wants a u.s intervention but the truth  is not all these candidates are members  of the cia or plotting against them  there was many of them were legitimate  even left-wing even left-wing candidates  and they were all imprisoned how can you  explain that  are you saying that all of them are cia  agents all of them are part of a  conspiracy  an individual like dora maria tellez was  a terrorist and she bombed buildings and  she had trucks of armed bandits the u.s  would put those individuals in jail or  maybe they wouldn't because we have the  case of january 6th but no people is  allowed to lead a violent coup against a  democratically elected government as we  saw in 2018 but they resisted that proxy  war  michael let me ask you um at his  inauguration president ortega announced  that nicaragua and china had just signed  a series of strategic agreements uh that  would include officially incorporating  nicaragua into beijing's global belt and  road initiative  as well as other trade programs  how much do you think that's going to  help nicaragua and how much does that  concern the united states  well look the united states obviously  there are global tensions with china and  i think uh china's  increasing influence and expansion in  all of latin america is something that's  certainly high on the agenda a political  policy agenda in the united states and  the united states  has to be  you know competitive with china and has  to make a better offer than than china i  just think that um the prospects for  economic development uh are not great no  matter who is involved in in nicaragua  given that incredible 